        "root_concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Physical Properties of Minerals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMOHS SCALE (1812) — comparative, not linear\n+----------------------------------------------------+\n|  1   Talc          scratched by fingernail         |\n|  2   Gypsum        scratched by fingernail         |\n|  2.5 ————————————— fingernail threshold ————————   |\n|  3   Calcite       scratched by copper coin        |\n|  3.5 ————————————— copper coin threshold ————————  |\n|  4   Fluorite      scratched by steel nail         |\n|  5   Apatite       scratched by steel knife        |\n|  5.5 ————————————— steel knife threshold ————————  |\n|  6   Orthoclase    scratched by window glass       |\n|  6.5 ————————————— window glass threshold ———————— |\n|  7   Quartz        scratches window glass easily   |\n|  8   Topaz         scratches quartz                |\n|  9   Corundum      scratches topaz                 |\n| 10   Diamond       scratches everything            |\n+----------------------------------------------------+"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:06-physical-properties, git-history:mineralogy:06-physical-properties]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:physical-properties",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
