        "title": "Physical Properties of Minerals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**What controls hardness**: Bond strength and type. Diamond (3D covalent carbon) = hardest. Talc (Mg phyllosilicate with only Van der Waals between layers) = softest. Ionic minerals fall in between."
    },
