      "text": "## Cleavage and Fracture"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md#016",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:06-physical-properties, git-history:mineralogy:06-physical-properties]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:physical-properties",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Physical Properties of Minerals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Cleavage** = tendency to break along specific crystallographic planes — planes where bond density is lowest or bond strength is weakest."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md#017",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:06-physical-properties, git-history:mineralogy:06-physical-properties]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:physical-properties",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physical, properties]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Physical Properties of Minerals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCLEAVAGE QUALITY DESCRIPTORS\n  Perfect    → smooth, mirror-like planes; very easy to produce\n  Good       → smooth but with some irregularity\n  Distinct   → recognizable but rough\n  Poor       → barely visible, mineral tends to fracture instead\n  None       → no cleavage; fracture only"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md#018",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:06-physical-properties, git-history:mineralogy:06-physical-properties]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/06-PHYSICAL-PROPERTIES.md",
